LEG 1 — G1 paste handling in AssetForm.tsx (touched file):
- added window-level `paste` listener in a useEffect (native ClipboardEvent), reads
  `e.clipboardData?.files`; only when `files.length` does it preventDefault + addFiles(files) — the same
  path dropped files use. Cleanup removes the listener on unmount.
- scope decision: WINDOW (with cleanup), not the form or drop zone. Rationale: the requirement is
  "anywhere the capture screen can receive keyboard focus"; the household <select> is outside the <form>
  but on the same screen, so a form-scoped handler would miss it. Evidence that a real paste event
  reaches it: the test fires the paste on the focusable display-name input (inside the screen) and it
  bubbles to the window handler and stages the file — see verify Section 3 test (a)/(d).
- text-only paste: no <input>-less content, files.length === 0 -> handler returns without preventDefault,
  nothing staged, no error (test (b)).
- pasted file staged as-is, never renamed (no naming logic); hint text changed to
  "Drag & drop photos here, click to select, or paste" — plain, promises no AI naming/derivation.

